FYLM 0.6 renames the dithering effect to FYLM Pixel Art. The effect match name FYLM_DitheringStudio and parameter ids 1-14 are unchanged, so this is a display-name change only; the upstream attribution above still applies to the ported dithering algorithms.

FYLM 0.11: 23 additional libretro/slang-shaders presets from commit a4f3aeec04fcb2624ec6df5dd17e38f9b575eab9 are included as test candidates. Dependency source headers and attribution evidence are under assets/ShaderGlass/Library/Sources and catalog-v1.json. Four FYLM portrait recipes change parameter defaults, not algorithm authorship. Per-shader public-release review remains pending. Original procedural thumbnail artwork is by FYLM; no user test artwork is distributed.

FYLM0.12: authored spatial YIQ tape extension and dynamic-signal.slang use NTSC signal concepts referenced against ntsc-rs commit8cfc51014092a6dc1da5eb0217bb9ae6516b124e; no Rust runtime or full NTSC decoder was ported. Existing Godot MIT lineage and frozen legacy shader retain prior attribution. New FYLM dynamic Slang sources are GPL-3.0-or-later. Source paths and distinctions: docs/vhs/RESEARCH-2026-11-02.md.

FYLM0.13 adds the crt-royale test candidate from the same pinned slang-shaders commit. Copyright(C)2014 TroggleMonkey; shader headers specify GPL-2.0-or-later. The original directory LICENSE.TXT, shader/include source and six mask textures are preserved under Assets/ShaderGlass/Library/Sources/crt/shaders/crt-royale. This does not assert that every other candidate has the same license. VHS and VHS mpalko resource candidates are tested locally but not newly embedded pending their own attribution review. The resource test BMP and GLSL fixture are original FYLM diagnostic data, not user artwork.
